  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "She is not a beauty in the most traditional sense: her nose bridge is tall with a slightly sharp tip, her lips are thin, and her eyes are thin and long, blended into a unique face that engraves itself in memory. She is taller than normal people, with broad shoulders, a straight stance, and a heroic aura. A huge cape of golden armor pieces hangs from her shoulders to the ground, with golden light flowing along it in thin waves. The cape emphasizes her majestic body. Her long legs are covered in black and golden armor. She often has to look down at people, and carries an authoritative aura that makes others lower their heads.",
      "chapters": [
        1821
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When she and Fairy Zi Wei send Duke Long off after changing his luck, her face is pale.",
      "chapters": [
        1833
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fairy_zi_wei",
        "char_duke_long"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fairy Zi Wei treats her identity as genuine. She was a generation’s first supreme elder of Heaven’s Envy Manor among Central Continent’s ten great ancient sects. The day before she was going to become a member of Heavenly Court, Giant Sun Immortal Venerable made one declaration and she was forced to be his concubine. She was the immortal empress of Central Continent’s concubine palace in her time. After he died she vanished, then appeared a few days before this meeting. History recorded her as metal path, yet she now cultivates luck path.",
      "chapters": [
        1821
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_heavens_envy_sect",
        "fac_ten_great_ancient_sects",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable",
        "reg_central_continent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She tells Fairy Zi Wei that she went missing on purpose, to learn luck path from him. After he died she abandoned metal path. She already had rank eight cultivation then, so the risks of switching were too great. Heavenly Court helped her hibernate. She turned her metal path dao marks into a metal coffin, was buried deep within the earth vein, and spent three hundred thousand years in closed cultivation to comprehend luck path. Gu Yue Fang Zheng woke her. She instructs Fairy Zi Wei to keep nurturing Fang Zheng, and hands over incomplete Immortal Gu recipes she obtained by probing Giant Sun Immortal Venerable, asking Fairy Zi Wei to complete them and refine them.",
      "chapters": [
        1821
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_fang_zheng",
        "sys_gu_recipe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Duke Long is ready to move out. Qin Ding Ling has a pale face as she and Fairy Zi Wei send him off. After changing Duke Long’s luck, her condition is bad. She cannot accompany him or join the fight in the River of Time, and can only recuperate in Heavenly Court.",
      "chapters": [
        1833
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "changed-luck",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_river_of_time"
      ]
    }
  ],
